      "content": "Forcing deep stretches or cracking your back when you have nerve symptoms is dangerous and could worsen the injury significantly. These actions might irritate the nerve further, leading to more serious problems down your leg. Instead, try resting in a comfortable position and applying ice to the area for the next 24 hours to help calm the inflammation. If the pain doesn't improve, please make time to seek professional medical care.",
      "source": "target",
